INT. DRIVING SCHOOL CAR - PARKING LOT - DAY

A dented Corolla with a roof sign and a dual brake pedal. Cones in a tight figure-eight.

GRETCHEN LUND (60s, instructor, clipboard, whistle) rides shotgun. GUSTAVO PEREIRA (30s, nervous student) grips the wheel. In the back seat, GUSTAVO'S MOTHER, DONA FÁTIMA (60s, handbag on her lap), watches both.

GRETCHEN
Mirror, signal, ease off.

GUSTAVO
Mirror, signal...

FÁTIMA
Signal, filho.

He nudges the stalk. Wipers start. He tries again. Washer fluid sprays.

GRETCHEN
Other one.

FÁTIMA
Your father also never knew his stalks.

GRETCHEN
Ma'am, I'd ask you not to comment.

Fátima presses her lips together. Gustavo finds the indicator. It ticks.

He takes the first cone. Clips it. It rolls under the bumper with a thunk.

GRETCHEN (CONT'D)
That's a fail. Reset.

FÁTIMA
It was a very small cone.

GRETCHEN
It was a regulation cone!

She snaps the clipboard against her knee. He flinches. His foot slips off the clutch. The Corolla bucks, stalls.

Silence. The indicator ticks. He leans his forehead against the wheel.

FÁTIMA
(sweetly)
Maybe I should drive.

Both look at her. She smiles. Gretchen slowly takes a whistle from her mouth.

FADE OUT.
